Z||000000||Andy||05-26-99||05:04 PM||||Just joint youre Forum.You all good some great stuff going on.Iguess i be hanging around.I'm planning to repaint my hole Fiero,current paint is black and in bad shape.Want to change it to dark red and use the basecoat ,clearcoat paint.Any thing I need to watch out for or do special, since it is a Fiberglass body.Thanks for any help
Z||000001||theogre||05-26-99||06:37 PM||||just remember to use extream care with sanding tools or you'll dig holes real quick.<p>watch what primer, and paint you use. some aren't flexible or sticky enough for the soft nose & tail surfaces. 
Z||000002||Gokart||05-27-99||07:15 PM||||When I had an 84 coupe a few years back I painted it twice! First color was teal and it was nicknamed "runs", a learning experience! The 2nd time around I painted it red-raspberry mettalic and it came out great! Very light sanding is great advice. Also mask, mask, mask. Do very thin coats. I just used standard primer and didn't bother with flexible parts paint, it stayed on fine. If you have a NAPA around where you live, they will supply you with the rental equipment and some advice. One more thing, make sure if you do it in a garage you blow out and clean all dust! Good luck!
